{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q424328","formula":"Pb₅(AsO₄)₃Cl","hill":"As3ClO12Pb5","elements":["O","Cl","As","Pb"],"composition":{"O":12.0,"As":3.0,"Cl":1.0,"Pb":5.0},"names":{"en":"Mimetite","ru":"Миметизит","uk":"Міметезит"},"descriptions":{"en":"Mimetite is a lead arsenate chloride mineral (Pb5(AsO4)3Cl) which forms as a secondary mineral in lead deposits, usually by the oxidation of galena and arsenopyrite. The name derives from the Greek Μιμητής mimetes, meaning \"imitator\" and refers to mimetite's resemblance to the mineral pyromorphite. This resemblance is not coincidental, as mimetite forms a mineral series with pyromorphite (Pb5(PO4)3Cl) and with vanadinite (Pb5(VO4)3Cl).","ru":"Мимети́т, или миметизи́т (также встречается миметези́т) — минерал из класса фосфатов, арсенатов, ванадатов, образующий редкие скопления обычно зелёных призматических кристаллов в зонах окисления месторождений свинцовых и свинцово-цинковых руд.","uk":"Міметезит (рос. миметезит; англ. mimetesite; нім."},"fame":22,"pubchemCid":71300916,"mass":1490.0,"charge":0,"smiles":"[O-][As](=O)([O-])[O-].[O-][As](=O)([O-])[O-].[O-][As](=O)([O-])[O-].[Cl-].[Pb+2].[Pb+2].[Pb+2].[Pb+2].[Pb+2]","inchikey":"TYYHXOUGFIRONY-UHFFFAOYSA-D","iupac":"pentakis(lead(2+));triarsorate;chloride","classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-566301","atoms":84,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[10.455,0.0,0.0],[0.0,7.587,0.0],[-10.446,0.0,18.163]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":-3.678,"y":5.643,"z":13.879,"el":"As"},{"x":-0.351,"y":1.94,"z":1.048,"el":"As"},{"x":0.36,"y":5.647,"z":17.115,"el":"As"},{"x":-1.537,"y":1.849,"z":13.366,"el":"As"},{"x":-0.747,"y":1.938,"z":8.259,"el":"As"},{"x":0.756,"y":5.649,"z":9.904,"el":"As"},{"x":1.545,"y":5.738,"z":4.798,"el":"As"},{"x":3.686,"y":1.944,"z":4.284,"el":"As"},{"x":-5.574,"y":1.853,"z